n communicating. Conscientious and stress handling good. Weather assessment important for long-distance. Computer skills good. Communication tone issue may affect crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills. Strength: quick correct decisions, attention. Concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education (lack of adaptability). Concern for others is good for crew cooperation. Egocentric may conflict.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as a loner. Strengths: problem solving, concentration, responsibility. Concerns: moody, loner may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe need best overall fit. Likely candidate B seems balanced: stress resilience, conscientiousness, weather assessment, computer skills. Communication tone issue but can be coached. Candidate A has leadership but unfriendly. Candidate C has decision speed but communication issues and egocentric. Candidate D has responsibility but moody/loner.\n\nThus I might recommend Candidate B. Provide argument referencing facts. Also note that we haven't discussed all candidates yet, but we can start with B. Provide recommendation.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote.\n\nProceed."}
